101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 61 0 R
/T (A controlled CPU-bound workload is executed by multiple Python worker processes. Three affinity modes are compared: none \(the Linux scheduler chooses placement\), spread \(each worker is restricted to one available logical CPU\), and single \(all workers are restricted to one available logical CPU as a parallelism-reduction control\). Three distribution strategies are compared: block, round-robin \(rr\), and dynamic shared-queue distribution. The program records elapsed time, throughput, worker-time imbalance, worker CPU time, and per-worker context-switch counters exposed by /proc/self/status. Optional Linux tools provide independent process, scheduler, and migration observations.)
/E (A controlled CPU-bound workload is executed by multiple Python worker processes. Three affinity modes are compared: none \(the Linux scheduler chooses placement\), spread \(each worker is restricted to one available logical CPU\), and single \(all workers are restricted to one available logical CPU as a parallelism-reduction control\). Three distribution strategies are compared: block, round-robin \(rr\), and dynamic shared-queue distribution. The program records elapsed time, throughput, worker-time imbalance, worker CPU time, and per-worker context-switch counters exposed by /proc/self/status. Optional Linux tools provide independent process, scheduler, and migration observations.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
