/T (This CA-5 report applies the original multi-core scheduling research topic to a real Linux systems-engineering investigation. It defines controlled experiments for processor affinity, workload distribution and worker-count scaling; provides a Python multiprocessing implementation; and identifies Linux interfaces for observing CPU placement and context switching. The final engineering conclusion must be written after collecting the actual benchmark data. Until then, the report presents hypotheses and a reproducible measurement procedure rather than claiming a performance result.)
/E (This CA-5 report applies the original multi-core scheduling research topic to a real Linux systems-engineering investigation. It defines controlled experiments for processor affinity, workload distribution and worker-count scaling; provides a Python multiprocessing implementation; and identifies Linux interfaces for observing CPU placement and context switching. The final engineering conclusion must be written after collecting the actual benchmark data. Until then, the report presents hypotheses and a reproducible measurement procedure rather than claiming a performance result.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [22]
