/Title (Affinity is a constraint, not a command that guarantees faster execution. A spread policy can keep workers on distinct available CPUs and reduce migration, but it can also bind work to a CPU that is temporarily busy. The single policy intentionally restricts all workers to one allowed CPU; it is a control that demonstrates the cost of removing parallel execution capacity.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1041 0 R
/Prev 1081 0 R
>>
endobj
